<title>SWEDEN: SWEDISH RIKSBANK BOARD MEETING ENDS, NO RATE MOVES.</title>
<headline>SWEDISH RIKSBANK BOARD MEETING ENDS, NO RATE MOVES.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sweden's central bank, the Riksbank, ended its board meeting on Thursday with no changes announced to interest rates.</p>
<p>The market had not expected any moves.</p>
<p>The Riksbank's repo rate, its key tool for controlling money market liquidity, has stood at 4.10 percent since December 17.</p>
<p>Its other key rates, the deposit and lending rates, currently stand at 3.75 percent and 5.25 percen,t respectively.</p>
<p>The bank's board will next meet on August 28.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
</text>
